: 'This sh has no comment lexer: a # line is executed, and one carrying'
: 'shell metacharacters is a syntax error that kills the script.  See'
: 'cmd/sh/exec3.c:41 for the : builtin used here instead.'

: 'The daemon says how many connections it has when it starts -- inet:'
: 'ready, NN connections -- and it is fifteen on a machine with the'
: 'standard twenty descriptors.  A listening port is an open channel'
: 'whoever holds it, and the switchboard holds one per service.'
: 'What is started here spends seven of them: slip 1, and the services'
: 'enabled in /etc/inetd.conf -- echo, daytime, ntalk, telnet, finger,'
: 'shell, and smtp where a mail transport is installed.  Telnet costs one'
: 'of the seven and not three, so the switchboard serves as many logins at'
: 'once as it has children and free ptys, and ntalk costs one where the'
: 'standalone talkd cost two.'
: 'The mail transport takes one, through the smtp line in inetd.conf where'
: 'lists/mail-light.list put /etc/smtpd.  The eight left are what a game,'
: 'an ftp or an outgoing telnet has to draw on.'

IFADDR=10.0.0.2
IFMASK=255.255.255.0
SLIPLINE=/dev/tty51
NTPSERVER=10.0.0.1

/etc/mknod /dev/inet p
/etc/inet &
/etc/ifconfig $IFADDR $IFMASK
if /bin/test -r $SLIPLINE
then
	echo rc.net: starting slip on $SLIPLINE
	/etc/slip $SLIPLINE &
else
	echo rc.net: no $SLIPLINE, skipping slip
fi

if /bin/test -r /etc/sntp
then
	echo rc.net: setting the clock from $NTPSERVER
	/etc/sntp -t 5 -r 2 $NTPSERVER
fi

if /bin/test -r /etc/inetd
then
	if /bin/test -r /etc/inetd.conf
	then
		echo rc.net: starting inetd, the services in /etc/inetd.conf
		/etc/inetd &
	else
		echo rc.net: no /etc/inetd.conf, skipping inetd
	fi
fi

: 'telnetd, fingerd and remshd are not started here.  Each has an inetd'
: 'mode -- read the connection on standard input, answer on standard'
: 'output, one connection, exit -- so each is one line in /etc/inetd.conf'
: 'and nothing of it is resident between callers.'
: 'A site that wants one of them standalone runs it by hand'
: '(/etc/telnetd -m 3 &) and comments its line out of inetd.conf: the'
: 'same binary does both, and which it does is decided by whether the'
: 'switchboard put INETD_REMADDR in its environment.  Running both at'
: 'once is what must not happen -- the second passive open on the port is'
: 'refused and the port then answers whichever got there first.'

: 'talkd is not started here and no longer exists: ntalk is the switchboard'"'"'s'
: 'own ntalk line in /etc/inetd.conf.  A datagram service cannot be handed'
: 'to an exec'"'"'d program, so inetd answers it internally -- it binds 518 and'
: 'forks a child WITHOUT exec on the first datagram, and that child holds the'
: 'invitation table until it holds nothing.  So the state between datagrams'
: 'that made the old daemon resident is kept for as long as the protocol can'
: 'ask about it, and nothing is resident between calls.'

: 'smtpd is not started here: it is an inetd service, and its line in'
: '/etc/inetd.conf ships enabled.  The line is conditional even so --'
: 'smtpd comes from lists/mail-light.list while inetd.conf comes from'
: 'lists/net.list, and inetd does not offer a service whose program is'
: 'not installed -- so a machine with no mail transport binds no port 25'
: 'and nothing has to edit a file.  A site that wants the daemon'
: 'standalone runs /etc/smtpd -m 1 & here and comments that line out:'
: 'one holder of port 25, never two.'
